│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ param_sharing_pairwise_reduction                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 24 independent parameters per repetition (8 RY + 8 RZ_pre + 8     │
│                          │ RZ_post), giving 146 total trainable parameters while already achieving perfect           │
│                          │ train/val/test accuracy. Since the score heavily rewards parameter economy and the task   │
│                          │ is apparently easy enough to reach 100% accuracy, we can cut the parameter count roughly  │
│                          │ in half by sharing rotation angles across adjacent qubit pairs (0,1), (2,3), (4,5), (6,7) │
│                          │ for each of the RY, RZ_pre, and RZ_post layers. This preserves the same circuit           │
│                          │ structure, connectivity, and depth (so expressivity from entanglement is unchanged), but  │
│                          │ reduces the number of unique trainable parameters per repetition from 24 to 12, which     │
│                          │ should substantially raise parameter_efficiency while keeping accuracy high due to the    │
│                          │ apparent simplicity of the underlying task/encoding.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0415                                                                                   │
