│                          │ RZ‑post), giving 146 total trainable parameters for a circuit that already reaches        │
│                          │ perfect train/val/test accuracy — meaning most of that parameter budget is wasted and     │
│                          │ heavily penalizes the parameter‑economy score.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version keeps the essential per‑qubit expressivity (8 independent RY angles, since   │
│                          │ these directly shape the per‑qubit response to the fixed data encoding) but replaces the  │
│                          │ two full layers of 8 independent RZ angles with a **single shared RZ parameter** applied  │
│                          │ to all wires (a global phase‑style correction) and adds a **cross‑ring CRX entangling     │
│                          │ layer** using **one shared parameter** across 4 long-range pairs (0-4,1-5,2-6,3-7) to mix │
│                          │ information between the two halves of the register without adding extra trainable degrees │
│                          │ of freedom. The nearest‑neighbor CZ ring (no parameters) still provides local             │
│                          │ entanglement.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This cuts the parameter count per repetition from 24 down to 10 (8 RY + 1 shared RZ + 1   │
│                          │ shared CRX), roughly a 58% reduction, while preserving both local (CZ ring) and           │
│                          │ long‑range (CRX cross links) entanglement structure needed for expressivity. Fewer        │
│                          │ trainable parameters should shrink train/validation gap risk, speed convergence, and      │
│                          │ substantially boost the parameter‑efficiency term in the score while retaining            │
│                          │ near‑identical circuit depth/gate count and thus similar representational power.          │
