│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ remove_redundant_rz_pre_layer                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Since CZ is a diagonal gate, it commutes with any RZ rotation. In the current ansatz, an  │
│                          │ RZ layer is applied both before ("rz_pre_*") and after ("rz_post_*") the CZ entangling    │
│                          │ ladder on every wire. Because RZ and CZ are all diagonal in the computational basis, the  │
│                          │ two RZ layers on the same wire simply compose into a single effective RZ rotation (the CZ │
│                          │ in between doesn't change this), regardless of parameter values. This means the "rz_pre"  │
│                          │ layer adds zero expressive power beyond what "rz_post" already provides — it's pure       │
│                          │ parameter redundancy that hurts parameter economy without helping accuracy. Removing it   │
│                          │ cuts 8 parameters per repetition (48 total across the 6 repetitions), roughly halving the │
│                          │ RZ-related parameter count while preserving the full reachable unitary set, which should  │
│                          │ substantially improve the parameter-economy component of the score without harming        │
│                          │ accuracy.                                                                                 │
