│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ paired_shared_ring_longrange                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the strongest economy trick from each parent: (1) the "paired     │
│                          │ parameter sharing" scheme from the second seed program, where adjacent qubit pairs (0,1), │
│                          │ (2,3), (4,5), (6,7) share a single RY rotation parameter instead of each qubit having its │
│                          │ own, cutting the initial rotation-layer parameter count from 8 to 4; and (2) the          │
│                          │ shared-RZ + shared-CRX long-range entangling block from the current program, which adds   │
│                          │ global phase correction and half-register cross entanglement using only 1 parameter each  │
│                          │ rather than 8. The full CZ ring (including the wrap-around 7-0 connection) from the       │
│                          │ current program is kept to preserve full-register entanglement/expressivity with zero     │
│                          │ extra trainable cost since CZ has no parameters.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result is an ansatz with only 6 trainable parameters (4 paired RY + 1 shared RZ + 1   │
│                          │ shared CRX), roughly 8x-16x fewer parameters than the parent programs (50 and 62          │
│                          │ respectively), while retaining: (a) per-pair distinguishability from the encoding via     │
│                          │ distinct RY parameters for each qubit pair, (b) full nearest-neighbor + wraparound        │
│                          │ entangling connectivity via the CZ ring, (c) a global phase-correction layer via shared   │
│                          │ RZ, and (d) long-range half-register entanglement via shared CRX. Since both parent       │
│                          │ programs achieved perfect train/val/test accuracy (1.00) with far more parameters, and    │
│                          │ the score is dominated by parameter economy given matched accuracy, this extreme          │
│                          │ parameter reduction while preserving full connectivity and both local and long-range      │
│                          │ entangling structure should substantially improve parameter_efficiency and thus the       │
│                          │ combined score, provided the reduced-parameter circuit can still fit the small training   │
│                          │ set (which is plausible given the redundant/shared structure already showed no accuracy   │
│                          │ loss when going from 98 to 50 parameters in the seeds, and from 8 to 1 rz parameter in    │
│                          │ the current program).                                                                     │
