│ patch_description        │ Building on the trend that fewer trainable parameters have not hurt accuracy (50→62→74    │
│                          │ params all reach 1.0 accuracy with similar scores), this edit drastically cuts parameter  │
│                          │ count further while preserving both local and long-range entanglement structure. We keep  │
│                          │ the 4 shared-pair RY rotations (providing per-pair expressivity tied to the input         │
│                          │ encoding), replace the previous post-entangling RZ layer with a single shared long-range  │
│                          │ CRZ gate connecting the two halves of the register (0-4,1-5,2-6,3-7), and keep the CZ     │
│                          │ ring for nearest-neighbor entanglement. This reduces trainable parameters from 50 to just │
│                          │ 5 (an order-of-magnitude cut) while retaining full connectivity (local ring + cross-half  │
│                          │ links), which should further boost parameter efficiency and generalization without        │
│                          │ sacrificing training accuracy, since the earlier experiments show the underlying task is  │
│                          │ separable with very few parameters.                                                       │
