│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ close_cz_ring                                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a linear nearest-neighbor CZ chain (0-1,1-2,...,6-7), leaving     │
│                          │ qubits 0 and 7 disconnected. Closing this into a ring by adding a final CZ(7,0) gate      │
│                          │ creates a cyclic entangling topology, allowing information to flow between the two ends   │
│                          │ of the chain without adding any trainable parameters (CZ is parameter-free). This         │
│                          │ increases circuit expressivity and connectivity at essentially zero parameter cost, which │
│                          │ should help maintain or improve accuracy/generalization while keeping the excellent       │
│                          │ parameter economy (still 26 params) that already scores well.                             │
