│ patch_name               │ add_global_rx_and_extra_rz_bias                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the strongest prior architecture (global RY + ring-CZ entangler + global RZ,  │
│                          │ which scored 0.72 with only 14 trainable parameters), this edit further reduces parameter │
│                          │ count relative to the current 32-parameter candidate while adding two collective          │
│                          │ single-qubit rotations recommended for capturing global biases: a global RX applied to    │
│                          │ all qubits before the RY layer, and a second global RZ applied to all qubits after the    │
│                          │ existing RZ layer. The RX-before-RY pair is not redundant since RX and RY on the same     │
│                          │ qubit do not commute, giving each qubit an effective 2-parameter single-qubit rotation    │
│                          │ before entanglement — strictly more expressive than RY alone at a cost of only one extra  │
│                          │ shared parameter. The extra post-RZ layer models any residual global phase/bias that the  │
│                          │ measurement stage might be sensitive to, at the cost of one more shared parameter. Total  │
│                          │ unique parameters per repetition rises from 2 (in the 0.72-scoring seed) to 4, still far  │
│                          │ fewer than the current 32-parameter design, while retaining the ring entangler that       │
│                          │ worked well previously.                                                                   │
