│ patch_description        │ Revert to the more parameter-efficient 2-group RY/RZ sharing scheme (matching the         │
│                          │ best-performing seed: p_g0 for wires 0-3, p_g1 for wires 4-7), which achieved the top     │
│                          │ combined score (0.72) with only 14 params, shallow depth (29), and fast convergence (30   │
│                          │ steps) versus the current 4-group (26-param) version that scored lower (0.66).            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On top of that efficient backbone, apply the recommended enhancement: replace every       │
│                          │ second CZ in the entangling chain (links [0,1],[2,3],[4,5],[6,7]) with a parametrized XX  │
│                          │ rotation sharing a single new "xx_ent" parameter. This adds only 1 extra trainable        │
│                          │ parameter (15 total) while injecting tunable two-qubit interaction strength beyond the    │
│                          │ fixed CZ's fixed-angle entanglement, potentially improving expressivity/accuracy without  │
│                          │ meaningfully increasing depth or hurting convergence speed. The remaining links           │
│                          │ [1,2],[3,4],[5,6] stay as fixed CZ gates to preserve full-chain connectivity at zero      │
│                          │ extra parameter cost.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combines the best-known parameter-efficient rotation-sharing pattern with a          │
│                          │ minimal-cost, physically motivated entangler upgrade.                                     │
