│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ global_ry_crz_rz_share                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The previous variant introduced 5 unique parameters per block (4 RY-pair params + 1       │
│                          │ shared CRZ), giving n_params=32 and a lower combined score (0.65) than the simpler        │
│                          │ 2-parameter designs that reached 0.72. This suggests the extra RY granularity added       │
│                          │ parameter cost without accuracy gain.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Here we collapse the four RY-pair parameters into a single global RY parameter (as in the │
│                          │ best-performing seed), keep the fixed nearest-neighbor CZ chain for full connectivity,    │
│                          │ retain a single shared CRZ parameter for long-range (cross-register) entanglement to      │
│                          │ preserve extra expressivity beyond the pure-CZ seed, and add a global RZ layer to mix     │
│                          │ axes cheaply. This yields only 3 unique parameters per block (down from 5), directly      │
│                          │ improving parameter economy while keeping an entangling CRZ layer that the 2-parameter    │
│                          │ seeds lacked, which may help capture correlations with fewer training steps and a smaller │
│                          │ train/test gap.                                                                           │
