│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tri_axis_theta_rotation                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the current single-shared-parameter design (all rotations reuse "theta"), I   │
│                          │ add a third rotation axis (RX) before the existing RY layer, still reusing the same       │
│                          │ "theta" parameter. This creates a full RX-RY-CZ-entangle-RZ pattern per qubit, all driven │
│                          │ by one scalar angle, giving richer single-qubit rotations (covering all three Pauli axes) │
│                          │ without increasing the parameter count at all. Since RX and RY don't commute, inserting   │
│                          │ an RX layer before RY (with no entangling gate between them) changes the effective        │
│                          │ single-qubit unitary in a nontrivial way, potentially improving trainability/convergence  │
│                          │ speed and accuracy stability while keeping n_params=8, preserving the strong parameter    │
│                          │ economy that has been driving score improvements in previous generations.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0237                                                                                   │
