│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Simplify the rotation layer to use a single shared parameter "theta" for all pre- and     │
│                          │ post-entanglement rotations (matching the best-performing prior seed with n_params=8,     │
│                          │ score=0.80), and additionally inject a single shared-parameter CRZ layer on disjoint      │
│                          │ qubit pairs after the CZ ring, as recommended. This adds only one extra trainable         │
│                          │ parameter ("phi") per block repetition while giving the ansatz a tunable, parametrized    │
│                          │ two-qubit interaction strength beyond the fixed CZ entangler, which should improve        │
│                          │ expressivity/generalization without significantly increasing parameter count. Reducing    │
│                          │ rotation parameters from 4 groups to a single shared theta cuts parameter count roughly   │
│                          │ in half compared to the current program, directly improving parameter economy, while the  │
│                          │ added CRZ layer compensates for the lost per-qubit rotation flexibility via controlled    │
│                          │ entanglement tuning.                                                                      │
