                         Patch Metadata - Gen 34/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two 0.80-scoring seeds: keeps the extreme parameter economy of a single  │
│                          │ shared scalar "theta" driving every rotation (n_params = 8 total across the 8 block       │
│                          │ repetitions), while combining the best structural elements from both parents. From the    │
│                          │ RX+RY+RZ seed we take the richer per-qubit rotation sequence (RX then RY before           │
│                          │ entangling, RZ after), which gave the fastest convergence (60 steps). From the p_shared   │
│                          │ seed we take the denser dual-ring entangling topology (nearest-neighbor CZ ring + skip-2  │
│                          │ CZ ring, both with wrap-around), which gave the lowest validation/test loss (0.01) thanks │
│                          │ to higher connectivity. Combining both should retain the 1.00 accuracy with zero          │
│                          │ generalization gap while pushing for both fast convergence and low loss, at the same      │
│                          │ minimal 8-parameter budget as both parents (better parameter economy than the 14-param    │
│                          │ variant, which scored lower at 0.72).                                                     │
