                         Patch Metadata - Gen 35/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Builds on the two prior 1-parameter-per-block designs (candidate "theta" with RX/RY/RZ    │
│                          │ pre/post layers plus fixed CZ ring+diameter, and candidate "p_shared" with RY/RZ plus CZ  │
│                          │ ring+skip-2) that both reached score 0.80 but showed a trade-off: the                     │
│                          │ RX+RY+CZ-ring+CZ-diameter+RZ variant converged much faster (60 steps) than the            │
│                          │ RY+CZ-ring+CZ-skip2+RZ variant (240 steps), while both had identical accuracy and         │
│                          │ parameter count (8 total, 1 unique per block).                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the faster-converging variant used *two* non-commuting            │
│                          │ single-qubit rotation axes (RX then RY) before entangling, giving richer single-qubit     │
│                          │ expressivity per shared scalar, and used a *fixed* long-range entangler (diameter CZ).    │
│                          │ This version keeps that faster-converging single-qubit structure (RX, RY pre-layer; RZ    │
│                          │ post-layer, all reusing the same scalar "theta") but replaces one of the fixed long-range │
│                          │ CZ diameter gates with a *parametrized* CRZ entangler on antipodal pairs that reuses the  │
│                          │ SAME shared scalar "theta" as the rotation gates (per the recommendation). This turns the │
│                          │ previously "free" long-range entangling structure into a genuinely trainable,             │
│                          │ non-commuting two-qubit interaction, without adding a single extra trainable parameter    │
│                          │ (n_params stays fixed by the outer repetition count), potentially increasing the          │
│                          │ expressive power of the shared scalar and improving loss/generalization while preserving  │
│                          │ the fast-converging single-qubit backbone.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Gate budget is kept close to the best-performing prior variant (ring CZ for local         │
│                          │ connectivity + antipodal CRZ instead of antipodal CZ) to avoid unnecessary depth growth.  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0611                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
