│ patch_description        │ Replace the current two-parameter (theta, phi) design with a single-parameter "theta"     │
│                          │ ansatz that stacks two tri-axis rotation + dense-CZ (ring + antipodal) sub-blocks         │
│                          │ back-to-back inside one ansatz-block definition. This mirrors the best-performing prior   │
│                          │ seed (single shared theta driving RX/RY/RZ layers with a ring+antipodal CZ entangler,     │
│                          │ which achieved score 0.80 and fast convergence at 60 steps) but doubles the internal      │
│                          │ depth by repeating the rotate-entangle-rotate pattern twice, still reusing the same       │
│                          │ single trainable "theta" parameter throughout. The intuition (from the recommendation) is │
│                          │ that adding a second moderate-depth block with extreme parameter sharing increases        │
│                          │ expressivity/entangling power without adding any new trainable parameters, which should   │
│                          │ preserve or improve accuracy/generalization while further reducing the number of          │
│                          │ optimization steps needed to converge, at zero extra parameter cost. This also eliminates │
│                          │ the second "phi" parameter entirely, restoring parameter economy (1 unique parameter per  │
│                          │ block instead of 2), which should raise parameter_efficiency substantially compared to    │
│                          │ the current 0.72-score, 14-parameter candidate.                                           │
