│ patch_name               │ shared_theta_with_antipodal_crz                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Revert to a single shared parameter "theta" per block (as in the best-performing seed     │
│                          │ with n_params=8, score=0.80) instead of the two-group split that inflated n_params to 14  │
│                          │ and hurt the score. On top of that, inject a parametrized entangling layer using CRZ      │
│                          │ gates on antipodal qubit pairs, reusing the SAME shared "theta" parameter (no new         │
│                          │ parameter names introduced), as suggested by the recommendation. This should increase     │
│                          │ expressivity of the entangling structure beyond pure fixed CZ gates, without any increase │
│                          │ in trainable-parameter count, potentially improving accuracy/generalization/convergence   │
│                          │ while keeping parameter economy at its current best.                                      │
