│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ theta_shared_degree4_ring                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Builds on the current best (single shared parameter "theta" driving RX, RY, and RZ layers │
│                          │ on all 8 qubits, giving each qubit a full three-axis rotation from just one trainable     │
│                          │ scalar per repetition — the proven floor of n_params = 8 given the fixed 6-fold           │
│                          │ repetition and 2 fixed readout params). The entangling structure is enriched from the     │
│                          │ previous degree-3 graph (nearest-neighbor ring + antipodal diameter links) to a degree-4  │
│                          │ graph by additionally inserting fixed, zero-parameter "skip-2" CZ links (connecting qubit │
│                          │ i to qubit i+2). This denser fixed entangling graph increases the circuit's               │
│                          │ expressive/correlation power at absolutely no parameter cost, which should further        │
│                          │ accelerate convergence and improve robustness/generalization on very few training         │
│                          │ examples, while keeping parameter economy at the demonstrated optimum (n_params = 8).     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
