│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This candidate merges the two strongest parent designs. From the "theta" seed (score      │
│                          │ 0.80, convergence in 60 steps) it keeps the extreme parameter-economy trick of driving    │
│                          │ *all three* rotation axes (RX, RY, RZ) with a single shared scalar parameter `theta` per  │
│                          │ block repetition — this pre/post-entanglement multi-axis rotation with one parameter was  │
│                          │ empirically the fastest-converging design. From the `p_shared` ring+skip-2 seed it        │
│                          │ borrows the richer, still completely parameter-free, entangling topology.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The entangling layer is upgraded to a union of three fixed, non-parametric CZ patterns    │
│                          │ forming a small expander graph on the 8-qubit ring:                                       │
│                          │   - distance-1 edges (nearest-neighbor ring, from both parents),                          │
│                          │   - distance-2 "skip" edges (from the `p_shared` seed), and                               │
│                          │   - distance-4 "diameter" edges (from the `theta` seed).                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Together every qubit gets degree-3 (or 4) fixed entangling connectivity, maximizing       │
│                          │ expressivity/generalization at zero extra parameter cost, while the single shared `theta` │
│                          │ scalar keeps the trainable-parameter count as small as the best-performing prior          │
│                          │ candidates (1 unique name per block, matching the fastest-converging seed). This aims to  │
│                          │ combine the "fast convergence" property of the RX+RY+RZ single-parameter idea with the    │
│                          │ "denser fixed entanglement" property of the ring+skip topology, hopefully improving       │
│                          │ robustness/generalization while preserving parameter economy and convergence speed.       │
