│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ stacked_shared_theta_block                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current 26-parameter, 4-group design (score 0.66) with the proven             │
│                          │ single-shared-parameter "theta" tri-axis design (RX→RY→dense CZ ring+antipodal→RZ) that   │
│                          │ previously scored 0.80 with only 8 parameters, and then duplicate that entire block once  │
│                          │ more (reusing the same "theta" parameter) right after the first block's final RZ layer.   │
│                          │ This follows the recommendation that stacking a second shared-θ block with dense CZ       │
│                          │ connectivity can roughly halve convergence steps while keeping the parameter count fixed  │
│                          │ at 8, since all gates in both blocks reuse the identical single trainable parameter. This │
│                          │ should improve parameter economy (back to 8 params) and speed convergence relative to the │
│                          │ 26-param variant, while preserving the perfect train/val/test accuracy already observed.  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0351                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
