                         Patch Metadata - Gen 44/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ single_shared_param_with_antipodal_entangling                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The two previous 1-parameter designs (pure RY/RZ single-scalar and the RX+RY+CRZ+RZ       │
│                          │ single-"theta" design with ring+antipodal CZ entanglement) both achieved the best         │
│                          │ combined score (0.80) with only 8 total trainable parameters, while the current           │
│                          │ 2-parameter design (ry_global/rz_global) regressed to 0.72 with almost double the         │
│                          │ parameters (14) despite identical accuracy. This confirms that parameter economy          │
│                          │ dominates the score here and that adding a second independent parameter name hurts rather │
│                          │ than helps.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit collapses the current ansatz back to a single shared parameter "theta" reused   │
│                          │ across both the pre-entanglement RY layer and the post-entanglement RZ layer (matching    │
│                          │ the top-scoring 1-parameter designs), while also upgrading the entangling layer from a    │
│                          │ plain ring to a ring + antipodal-pair CZ topology. The antipodal edges give every qubit   │
│                          │ an additional long-range entangling partner at zero parameter cost, which in the second   │
│                          │ seed reduced convergence_step from 240 to 60 while keeping the same accuracy and score.   │
│                          │ Combining the single-parameter economy with the faster-converging entangling topology     │
│                          │ should recover the 0.80 score while also improving convergence speed relative to the      │
│                          │ original 1-parameter seed.                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0452                                                                                   │
