                         Patch Metadata - Gen 46/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ two_shared_params_theta1_theta2                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The 3-unique-parameter design (p_g0, p_g1, xx_ent) regressed the combined score to 0.68   │
│                          │ from the 0.80 achieved by the single-shared-parameter seed designs, primarily because     │
│                          │ parameter efficiency dropped (n_params went from 8 to 20). This suggests that increasing  │
│                          │ distinct parameter names hurts the score more than it helps accuracy, since accuracy was  │
│                          │ already saturated at 1.00 in all variants.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the recommendation, I revert to the parameter-economical single-shared-scalar   │
│                          │ structure of the best-performing seed, but introduce a second shared parameter "theta2"   │
│                          │ dedicated to the long-range entangling CRZ gates (distinct from the rotation-layer        │
│                          │ parameter "theta1"). This gives the entangling layer independent tunable strength from    │
│                          │ the local rotations while keeping the total unique-parameter count per block at just 2    │
│                          │ (versus 8 total with 8 repetitions), which should preserve the high parameter-efficiency  │
│                          │ and convergence speed of the seed while potentially improving expressivity enough to      │
│                          │ reduce validation/test loss further or improve robustness on harder splits.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Structure:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. RX layer on all 8 qubits, shared "theta1".                                             │
│                          │ 2. RY layer on all 8 qubits, shared "theta1" (same param, different axis -> effectively a │
│                          │ 2D rotation from one scalar).                                                             │
│                          │ 3. Fixed nearest-neighbor CZ ring (zero param cost) for local entanglement.               │
│                          │ 4. Antipodal CRZ entangler using new shared "theta2" (independent trainable long-range    │
│                          │ interaction strength).                                                                    │
│                          │ 5. RZ layer on all 8 qubits, shared "theta1", closing the block.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps depth/gate-count similar to the 0.80-scoring seeds while adding exactly one    │
│                          │ extra trainable scalar per block repetition, testing whether decoupling entangler         │
│                          │ strength from local rotation angle helps push past the 0.80 ceiling.                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
