│ patch_description        │ Reduce the ansatz to exactly two shared trainable parameters: "theta1" drives every       │
│                          │ single-qubit rotation (RX, RY, RZ layers), and "theta2" drives a parametrized entangling  │
│                          │ layer (CRZ) that is interleaved with a fixed CZ ring. This is a compromise between the    │
│                          │ 1-parameter seed (score 0.80, but potentially under-expressive) and the 26-parameter      │
│                          │ current version (score 0.66, over-parametrized). Giving the entangler its own free angle, │
│                          │ separate from the single-qubit rotation angle, lets the circuit learn distinct rotation   │
│                          │ vs. entanglement strengths while keeping parameter count minimal (n_params=2), which      │
│                          │ should improve parameter_efficiency and maintain high accuracy/generalization, boosting   │
│                          │ the combined score.                                                                       │
