│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_theta_dense_connectivity                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current 26-parameter ansatz (score 0.66) with a single-shared-parameter       │
│                          │ design inspired by the best-performing seed (score 0.80, n_params=8). The key insight     │
│                          │ from prior experiments is that parameter economy dominates the score: collapsing all      │
│                          │ rotation angles into one shared trainable scalar "theta" achieves perfect train/val/test  │
│                          │ accuracy while using far fewer parameters. I further densify the fixed (zero-parameter)   │
│                          │ entangling backbone by adding nearest-neighbor CZ ring + antipodal CZ "diameter" edges +  │
│                          │ skip-2 CZ edges, raising qubit connectivity degree from 2 to 4 at no parameter cost. This │
│                          │ follows the recommendation to append skip-2 CZ links after the nearest-neighbor/antipodal │
│                          │ motif, aiming to boost expressivity/generalization and potentially speed convergence      │
│                          │ while keeping parameter count minimal (single shared scalar "theta" reused across RX, RY, │
│                          │ RZ and a CRZ layer).                                                                      │
