│ patch_name               │ axis_specific_param_sharing                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single global "theta" parameter with four axis-specific shared parameters:    │
│                          │ "theta_rx" for the RX pre-rotation layer, "theta_ry" for the RY pre-rotation layer,       │
│                          │ "theta_rz" for the RZ post-rotation layer, and "theta_e" for the parametrized XX          │
│                          │ entangler in the ring. This breaks the single-scalar bottleneck (which forces RX, RY, RZ  │
│                          │ and the entangler to move together) while still using aggressive parameter sharing (only  │
│                          │ 4 unique names per block instead of one per gate). The extra tunability along each axis   │
│                          │ should allow the optimizer to find sharper decision boundaries, potentially reducing      │
│                          │ validation/test loss and convergence steps, while keeping the parameter count low and     │
│                          │ preserving the dense ring + skip-2 + antipodal connectivity backbone that achieved the    │
│                          │ best combined score so far (0.80).                                                        │
