│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate already reaches the parameter-economy floor (n_params=8, one shared │
│                          │ "theta" per repetition) and achieves perfect train/val/test accuracy with zero            │
│                          │ generalization gap. Among prior candidates with the same accuracy/param count, the        │
│                          │ variant with a longer, denser gate sequence per repetition (depth ~96) converged in only  │
│                          │ 30 steps versus 60-240 for shallower variants — extra non-commuting rotations/entanglers  │
│                          │ give the optimizer a smoother, more expressive loss landscape without adding any          │
│                          │ trainable parameters (still 1 unique name "theta" per repetition).                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the recommendation, I duplicate the core sequence (RX→RY→alternating CNOT/CZ    │
│                          │ ring→skip-2 CZ→antipodal CRZ→RZ) once more within the same block, all reusing "theta".    │
│                          │ This roughly doubles depth/gate count (targeting ~96-108 depth) while keeping n_params    │
│                          │ fixed at 8, aiming to reduce convergence_step_mean similarly to the fastest-converging    │
│                          │ prior variant (30 steps) while preserving the perfect accuracy and zero generalization    │
│                          │ gap already achieved.                                                                     │
