                         Patch Metadata - Gen 59/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ theta_shared_lite_entangler_hybrid                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This design crosses the two 0.80-scoring seeds that both used a *single* shared trainable │
│                          │ parameter "theta" per block repetition (maximal parameter economy, n_params=8 total       │
│                          │ across 8 reps). The first seed used a fixed CNOT/CZ ring plus a parametrized antipodal    │
│                          │ CRZ layer (depth 72, converges in 60 steps); the second seed used an XX/CZ alternating    │
│                          │ ring plus extra skip-2 and antipodal CZ shortcuts (depth 96, but converges much faster in │
│                          │ 30 steps thanks to the non-commuting parametrized XX interaction placed directly in the   │
│                          │ entangling ring).                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The crossover keeps the fast-converging ingredient (the alternating                       │
│                          │ parametrized-XX/fixed-CZ nearest-neighbor ring, reusing "theta") since that was the       │
│                          │ decisive factor separating 30-step vs 60-step convergence between the two                 │
│                          │ equally-accurate seeds. It drops the extra zero-parameter skip-2 sub-ring (2b) from the   │
│                          │ second seed, since the antipodal shortcuts (2c) already provide long-range connectivity,  │
│                          │ and the skip-2 ring only added depth/gate-count without changing convergence speed or     │
│                          │ accuracy. The result should retain the 30-step convergence advantage while being          │
│                          │ shallower and having fewer gates than either 0.80 seed, improving the "PARAMETER ECONOMY" │
│                          │ / gate-count / depth aspects of the score without sacrificing the perfect train/val/test  │
│                          │ accuracy both seeds already achieve with only 1 trainable parameter per repetition.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Structure per block repetition (single shared parameter "theta"):                         │
│                          │ 1. RX on all 8 qubits (shared theta) — non-commuting pre-rotation axis 1.                 │
│                          │ 2. RY on all 8 qubits (shared theta) — non-commuting pre-rotation axis 2.                 │
│                          │ 3. Nearest-neighbor ring, alternating: even links get a parametrized XX(theta)            │
│                          │ interaction, odd links get a fixed, zero-parameter CZ. This is the key ingredient tied to │
│                          │ fast (30-step) convergence.                                                               │
│                          │ 4. Fixed, zero-parameter antipodal shortcuts (distance-4 on the 8-cycle) for long-range   │
│                          │ connectivity, kept lightweight (only 4 gates) instead of adding a second skip-2 sub-ring. │
│                          │ 5. RZ on all 8 qubits (shared theta) — post-entanglement rotation, reusing the same       │
│                          │ single parameter to keep the unique-parameter count at exactly 1 per block.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps n_params identical to both parents (1 unique name x 8 repetitions = 8 total),  │
│                          │ but removes 8 redundant CZ gates (the skip-2 sub-ring) per repetition, reducing           │
│                          │ depth/gate-count relative to the faster-converging parent while preserving its structural │
│                          │ advantage.                                                                                │
