│ patch_name               │ skip2_parametrized_cry_shared_theta_e                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Revert to the higher-scoring single-shared-parameter design (seed variant that reached    │
│                          │ combined score 0.80 with fast 30-step convergence), and enrich its zero-parameter skip-2  │
│                          │ sub-ring with a parametrized CRY interaction that reuses a single new shared parameter    │
│                          │ "theta_e". This keeps parameter count minimal (2 unique names per block instead of the    │
│                          │ current program's 2 names but with worse-performing RY/RZ-only design) while adding a     │
│                          │ non-commuting tunable long-range interaction that should improve                          │
│                          │ expressivity/generalization without hurting parameter economy. The design restores the    │
│                          │ alternating XX/CZ ring and antipodal CZ shortcuts from the best-performing prior          │
│                          │ candidate, and only changes the previously fixed CZ skip-2 links into CRY gates sharing   │
│                          │ "theta_e", per the recommendation.                                                        │
