│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the highest-scoring prior design (single shared "theta" parameter driving     │
│                          │ RX/RY/RZ layers plus an alternating XX/CZ nearest-neighbor ring, which achieved combined  │
│                          │ score 0.80 with fast 30-step convergence), I replace the current 20-parameter, group-of-8 │
│                          │ RY/RZ design (score 0.68) with that stronger topology, and additionally enrich the        │
│                          │ lightweight skip-2 sub-ring by replacing its zero-parameter CZ gates with parametrized    │
│                          │ CRY gates that all reuse a single new shared parameter "theta_e". This keeps the total    │
│                          │ trainable-parameter count at just 2 (theta, theta_e) — far fewer than the current 20 —    │
│                          │ while adding genuine tunable expressivity to the skip-2 connections instead of fixed CZ,  │
│                          │ which should help maintain full train/val/test accuracy with even better parameter        │
│                          │ economy and comparable or better convergence speed, since the skip-2 interactions can now │
│                          │ be optimized rather than fixed.                                                           │
