│ patch_description        │ Add a second, deeper entangling sub-block directly after the existing RZ layer, fully     │
│                          │ reusing the same shared "theta" parameter (no new parameter name introduced, so total     │
│                          │ trainable parameter count stays at n_params=8 across the 8 repetitions). The added        │
│                          │ sub-block follows the recommended structure: RX→RY(theta) rotation layer, alternating     │
│                          │ XX(theta)/CZ nearest-neighbor ring, a lightweight skip-2 CZ sub-ring, antipodal           │
│                          │ CZ/CRX(theta) shortcuts, and a closing RZ(theta) layer. This roughly doubles              │
│                          │ expressivity/depth (~+10-40 depth, staying well below the 114-depth ceiling) while        │
│                          │ preserving perfect parameter economy, aiming to reduce convergence steps as seen in prior │
│                          │ compact-block duplications.                                                               │
