│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ crY_skip2_subring                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed, zero-parameter skip-2 CZ sub-ring (step 2b) with a trainable CRY       │
│                          │ interaction on the same qubit pairs, sharing a single new parameter "theta_e". This turns │
│                          │ a previously static, non-trainable entangling layer into a lightweight, trainable one,    │
│                          │ adding only one extra parameter (total 2) while boosting local expressivity in the same   │
│                          │ low-depth topology that previously gave fast (30-step) convergence in related variants.   │
│                          │ Since CRY is not diagonal like CZ, it should provide richer entangling dynamics for the   │
│                          │ same gate count, potentially improving convergence speed and robustness without harming   │
│                          │ parameter economy much.                                                                   │
