                         Patch Metadata - Gen 69/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ decouple_entangler_param                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce a second shared trainable parameter "theta_e" dedicated exclusively to the      │
│                          │ parametrized two-qubit entangling gates (the ring's XX interactions and the antipodal CRX │
│                          │ interaction), while keeping the single shared "theta" for all single-qubit RX/RY/RZ       │
│                          │ rotations. This decouples the local-rotation angle from the entangling-interaction angle, │
│                          │ giving the optimizer an extra degree of freedom to independently tune how much "mixing"   │
│                          │ happens on-site versus across qubits. Prior work on parametrized quantum circuits shows   │
│                          │ that entangling-gate angles often need a different optimal scale than local rotation      │
│                          │ angles; forcing them to share one parameter can create a suboptimal trade-off that hurts  │
│                          │ convergence speed and expressivity. Splitting them into two shared parameters keeps the   │
│                          │ parameter count essentially unchanged in relative terms (going from 1 to 2 unique         │
│                          │ parameter names) while directly targeting the class of gates most responsible for shaping │
│                          │ entanglement/expressivity, which should improve accuracy stability and reduce required    │
│                          │ training steps without meaningfully harming parameter economy.                            │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0892                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 3; deleted: 0; modified: 10;                                                       │
