│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ xx_yy_entangler_ring                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed, zero-parameter CZ gates in the nearest-neighbor entangling ring with a │
│                          │ parametrized YY(theta) gate (reusing the same shared "theta" parameter used everywhere    │
│                          │ else). This turns the ring into an alternating XX(theta)/YY(theta) pattern instead of     │
│                          │ XX(theta)/CZ. Since XX and YY are non-commuting Ising interactions, alternating them      │
│                          │ under the same shared parameter enriches the entangling structure and mixing power of the │
│                          │ circuit without adding any new trainable parameters (still just 1 parameter, "theta").    │
│                          │ This directly extends the successful alternating-entangler motif that gave the best       │
│                          │ combined score (0.80) and fastest convergence in prior single-block variants, now applied │
│                          │ inside the compact block-building function used for both stacked repetitions.             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
