                         Patch Metadata - Gen 71/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The double-block stacking (calling `_add_theta_block` twice) kept the same combined score │
│                          │ (0.80) as the single-block version but roughly doubled depth/gate-count and quadrupled    │
│                          │ the convergence steps (120 vs 30), which is strictly worse for parameter/step economy.    │
│                          │ Revert to a single full `_add_theta_block` call (matching the best-converging prior       │
│                          │ variant) and instead add a *lightweight, localized* fractional duplication restricted to  │
│                          │ only 4 of the 8 qubits (wires 0-3), reusing the same shared "theta" parameter. This       │
│                          │ targeted local RX→RY→(XX/CZ ring)→RZ sub-pass sharpens correlations among a subset of     │
│                          │ qubits at a fraction of the gate-count cost of a full second block, aiming to preserve    │
│                          │ the fast (~30-step) convergence and low depth of the single-block design while            │
│                          │ potentially improving accuracy/generalization via the extra localized non-linearity, with │
│                          │ zero additional trainable parameters.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Argumentation: Since parameter count is already minimal (1 shared parameter, 8 total due  │
│                          │ to per-block instantiation) and the score is dominated by parameter economy and few-shot  │
│                          │ generalization, the marginal cost of the fractional block is small (16 extra gates on 4   │
│                          │ qubits vs 240 extra gates for a full second block), while it still deepens the circuit    │
│                          │ non-uniformly, which can help expressivity without hurting convergence speed as much as   │
│                          │ full duplication did.                                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0624                                                                                   │
