│ patch_description        │ Revert to the single-shared-parameter design (8 params total) that previously achieved    │
│                          │ the best combined score (0.80), and apply the recommended enhancement: replace the        │
│                          │ alternating XX(theta)/CZ nearest-neighbor entangling ring with an alternating             │
│                          │ XX(theta)/YY(theta) ring (still sharing the single "theta" parameter, zero new params).   │
│                          │ Using two non-commuting Ising interactions instead of one Ising + one fixed CZ increases  │
│                          │ the entangling expressivity of the ring without increasing parameter count, which should  │
│                          │ improve accuracy/generalization while preserving the excellent parameter economy and fast │
│                          │ convergence of the earlier 0.80-scoring seed. The current 14-parameter two-theta design   │
│                          │ underperformed (0.72), so we discard it in favor of the proven 8-parameter architecture   │
│                          │ plus this targeted entangler improvement.                                                 │
