                         Patch Metadata - Gen 78/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Builds on the previous single-shared-parameter (`theta`) design, which already reached    │
│                          │ perfect train/val/test accuracy with only 8 trainable parameters (one per outer           │
│                          │ repetition) and the fastest observed convergence (30 steps) among high-scoring            │
│                          │ candidates. The core block (RX→RY→alternating XX/CZ nearest-neighbor ring→skip-2          │
│                          │ sub-ring→antipodal shortcuts→RZ) is kept unchanged since it is proven to work well and is │
│                          │ parameter-optimal (a single shared angle drives every rotation and every non-fixed        │
│                          │ entangler).                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The only structural change is the addition of a lightweight, zero-parameter skip-3 CZ     │
│                          │ sub-ring (distance-3 links: 0-3, 2-5, 4-7, 6-1) right after the existing skip-2 and       │
│                          │ antipodal shortcuts inside the main block. This gives an additional layer of long-range,  │
│                          │ fixed connectivity (complementing the skip-2 and skip-4/antipodal links already present)  │
│                          │ at a cost of only 4 extra fixed two-qubit gates and no new trainable parameters, which    │
│                          │ should help spread correlations across the whole register more evenly and can improve     │
│                          │ generalization / robustness on very small training sets without affecting parameter       │
│                          │ economy.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The redundant fractional half-register block from the previous version is dropped (it     │
│                          │ duplicated rotation+entangling work on wires 0-3 without adding new connectivity types),  │
│                          │ trimming depth/gate-count while keeping the same trainable-parameter count (theta only,   │
│                          │ still 8 total after the fixed number of outer repetitions). This should preserve or       │
│                          │ improve the perfect accuracy and fast convergence while reducing depth and gate count,    │
│                          │ and keeping n_params minimal.                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0791                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
