                         Patch Metadata - Gen 79/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ single_block_with_midentangle_ry                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz repeats the entire theta-block twice (once globally, once restricted   │
│                          │ to wires 0-3), which roughly doubles depth and gate count (138 vs 72) without any         │
│                          │ measurable score improvement (both score 0.80, identical accuracy/convergence). Since     │
│                          │ parameter economy and low depth/gate-count are explicitly rewarded, this redundant second │
│                          │ pass is pure overhead. I remove the extra fractional block to return to the leaner        │
│                          │ single-block depth (~72), and instead inject the recommended additional non-commuting     │
│                          │ RY(theta) rotation layer in the middle of the entangling topology (between the skip-2     │
│                          │ sub-ring and the antipodal shortcuts) — this adds expressivity via an extra rotation axis │
│                          │ at the heart of the entangler stack without introducing any new trainable parameter (it   │
│                          │ reuses "theta"), and without the depth/gate cost of a full duplicated block. This should  │
│                          │ preserve the 1.0 accuracy and 8-parameter economy while significantly cutting depth and   │
│                          │ gate count, improving the efficiency-sensitive part of the score.                         │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0403                                                                                   │
